  "description": "Expose CQRS Commands and Queries as Model Context Protocol (MCP) tools over the Streamable HTTP transport, in the same delegate-first style as MapCommand/MapQuery. Tool calls dispatch in-process over MediatR's IMediator and run through the same validation/logging/cache/lock/enricher pipeline. Call MapMcp() to serve the tools; the endpoint coexists with MapCommand/MapQuery/MapAgent.\nCommonly used types:\nCnblogs.Architecture.Ddd.Cqrs.Mcp.CqrsInjectorExtensions\nCnblogs.Architecture.Ddd.Cqrs.Mcp.CqrsMcpEndpointExtensions\nCnblogs.Architecture.Ddd.Cqrs.Mcp.CqrsMcpToolGroup\nCnblogs.Architecture.Ddd.Cqrs.Mcp.CqrsMcpToolCollection",
